ent-AdvancedSterileScalpel = surgical scalpel
    .desc = A reusable surgical access instrument. Reprocess after contact with a patient.
ent-AdvancedSterileHemostat = vascular hemostat
    .desc = Controls internal bleeding through an open surgical access.
ent-AdvancedInstrumentSterilizationKit = instrument reprocessing pack
    .desc = Single-use cleaner and sterile wrap. Apply to a contaminated instrument; reprocessing takes five seconds.
ent-AdvancedClinicalBloodAnalyzer = portable blood analyzer
    .desc = Apply to an identified sample. Prints a biochemical profile at collection time, rather than the patient's current condition.
ent-AdvancedPortableXRay = portable X-ray scanner
    .desc = Examines the selected region for fractures, fixation and foreign bodies. Does not diagnose soft-tissue diseases.
ent-AdvancedElectrocardiograph = portable electrocardiograph
    .desc = Records cardiac rate in the chest region and compares it with the patient's baseline.
surgery-tool-sterile = Sterile instrument. Patient contact, striking something or dropping it breaks sterility.
surgery-tool-contaminated = Contaminated instrument. Apply an instrument reprocessing pack before surgery.
surgery-sterilize-first = Reprocess the instrument with a sterile pack first.
surgery-tool-ready = Instrument reprocessed and ready for surgery.
advanced-health-minigame-hint-incision = Hold at the start of the line and slowly guide the scalpel along the path. Release at the end. Slips injure tissue; resume from the marked point.
advanced-health-minigame-hint-vessels = Grip the highlighted vessel, hold until this stage fills, then release. Treat three sites. Moving the clamp away injures the vessel.
advanced-health-minigame-feedback-incision = Guide the scalpel along the marked incision
advanced-health-minigame-feedback-clamp-vessel = Hold the clamp on the vessel, then release
